course: dictionary
lesson: 8595
title: Reading a scoreboard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scoreboard is a large board or screen that shows the score in a game or match. Its numbers are information you can use. They show points, runs, goals and time. «The scoreboard shows overs and balls: 12.3 overs means 12 full overs and 3 balls of the next one.» That is a number code you can read.
explain: To find a difference, subtract the smaller score from the bigger one. To find a total, add the scores together. Always check which number belongs to which team before you calculate.
explain: A scoreboard does not always tell the whole story. «In a single game luck, bounces and goalkeepers can decide the score, so the scoreboard doesn't always show who played better.» The score shows what happened, not every reason why.
fact: A scoreboard is a large board or screen that shows the score in a game or match.
fact: A scoreboard can show points, runs, goals and time.
fact: In cricket, 12.3 overs means 12 full overs and 3 balls of the next over.
fact: Players put points on the scoreboard as the game goes on.
fact: A digital scoreboard shows the score on a screen instead of a board.
exercise: «The scoreboard shows 5 goals for the red team and 2 for the blue team.» How many more goals has the red team scored? | 5 | *3 | 2 | 7
exercise: «The scoreboard shows overs and balls: 12.3 overs means 12 full overs and 3 balls of the next one.» How many full overs does 12.3 show? | *12 | 15 | 123 | 3
exercise: What does a scoreboard show? | The names of the referees only | The rules of a game in full | *The score in a game or match | The weather for the day
test: «In a single game luck, bounces and goalkeepers can decide the score, so the scoreboard doesn't always show who played better.» What does this sentence teach? | Goalkeepers do not matter | *Scores show what happened, but not always who played best | The scoreboard always shows who played best | Luck never affects a game
test: The scoreboard shows 34 points for Team A and 27 for Team B. What is the difference between the two scores? | 6 | 61 | 8 | *7
exam: The scoreboard shows 18 points for Team A and 25 for Team B. What is the total of both scores? | *43 | 7 | 33 | 53
